{"baseRefOid":"b6f7c9b0f6b84ffe496719e39f2d2ba52d5ed3ac","body":"Paged readers need to retain small sealed updates without rebuilding the entire\nbase. Add chronological paged generations and a resident mutable batch whose\nretained snapshots expose one guarded effective RDF 1.2 view.\n\nCloses #457.\n\n- Resolve independent source dictionaries by value; apply ordered removals,\n  reinsertion and graph-scoped RDF 1.2 classification through indexed paging.\n- Pin every source descriptor and resident batch behind shared limits, caching,\n  qualified receipts and sticky operational failures.\n- Fold into canonically partitioned native pages with actual eager carrier-byte\n  identity, and expose the API through the supported RDF/umbrella facades.\n\nValidation executed: 82 core paging/graph integration tests, 42 mutable and 23\nglobal unit tests; 32 evaluator integration tests; the root facade smoke; and the\nrunnable consumer demonstrating retained/current answers and eager carrier parity.\nAll-target clippy with warnings denied and release wasm library compilation passed\nfor core, evaluator, RDF and umbrella packages. Refreshed helper hygiene, effective\nbuild-profile hygiene, formatting and whitespace passed. Independent Task 1 and\nTask 2 reviews passed; both signed commits passed their normal hooks.\n\nWasm compilation is established; wasm runtime execution and hosted CI are pending.\nStorage/log policy, depth scheduling and atomic publication remain caller-owned as\nspecified by the issue. Retained dictionaries have documented linear snapshot and\npotential cumulative quadratic costs; this change makes no throughput claim.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added layered paged datasets with insertions, removals, named graphs, snapshots, and compaction into canonical pages.\n  * Added SPARQL querying over paged stacks, including query limits and source-aware operation evidence.\n  * Added an example demonstrating edits across snapshots and queries.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Documented expected behavior for paged stacks, snapshots, queries, and compaction.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","headRefOid":"8364b29c9fb70195f123e2bc084160d83f78850a","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-06T21:26:24Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37532186299/job/112504322734","name":"workspace","startedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:02Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:09Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37532180965/job/112504041923","name":"Analyze (actions)","startedAt":"2026-10-06T21:12:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CodeQL"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-06T21:17:52Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37532186301/job/112504054814","name":"Build The PurRDF Book","startedAt":"2026-10-06T21:12:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Docs"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37532180965/job/112504042057","name":"Analyze (c-cpp)","startedAt":"2026-10-06T21:12:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CodeQL"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:30Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37532180965/job/112504041887","name":"Analyze (javascript-typescript)","startedAt":"2026-10-06T21:12:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CodeQL"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:31Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37532180